WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.720
- Can you file a lawsuit in
the form of a comic book?

00:00:03.720 --> 00:00:06.320
Well, the answer is apparently yes.

00:00:06.320 --> 00:00:10.120
In a case in Texas, a suit
between a comic book store

00:00:10.120 --> 00:00:13.270
and a hotel next door, there
was a third amended complaint.

00:00:13.270 --> 00:00:15.750
So the plaintiff apparently
filed some motions

00:00:15.750 --> 00:00:17.430
saying that they needed
more clarification.

00:00:17.430 --> 00:00:20.470
And in response to that, the
plaintiffs got really cheeky

00:00:20.470 --> 00:00:23.900
and they filed their complaint
effectively as a comic book.

00:00:23.900 --> 00:00:24.880
Halfway through the complaint,

00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:28.060
it basically just switches
to an illustrated comic

00:00:28.060 --> 00:00:30.560
and they explain all of the events

00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:33.020
that involve basically a
bunch of patrons in the hotel

00:00:33.020 --> 00:00:35.590
throwing large metal
canisters off the hotel

00:00:35.590 --> 00:00:38.820
and into the comic book store
in the form of a comic book.

00:00:38.820 --> 00:00:39.653
Will this work?

00:00:39.653 --> 00:00:42.020
That remains to be seen,
but it is hilarious

00:00:42.020 --> 00:00:43.320
and incredibly interesting.

00:00:43.320 --> 00:00:44.550
I've never seen this one before.

00:00:44.550 --> 00:00:46.553
So we'll see this comic book in court.

